 "intro": "Genres, the parts of a story, and the verbs for talking and writing about books.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "argumento",
   "significado": "plot",
   "pron": "ar-gu-MEN-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is the plot of a book or film. In a debate, «argumento» is also a reason, never a quarrel.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "narrador",
   "significado": "narrator",
   "pron": "na-rra-DOR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It may speak in the first person («yo») or the third («él»). It is not the same as the author.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "relato",
   "significado": "short story, tale",
   "pron": "rre-LA-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is shorter than a novel. «Relato» and «cuento» are used almost the same. It comes from «relatar», to tell.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "leyenda",
   "significado": "legend",
   "pron": "le-YEN-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The ll sounds like y: le-YEN-da. It passes by word of mouth and nobody knows how much is true.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ensayo",
   "significado": "essay",
   "pron": "en-SA-yo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Careful: «ensayo» is also the rehearsal of an orchestra or a play. Check the context.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "capítulo",
   "significado": "chapter",
   "pron": "ka-PI-tu-lo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent on the i: ca-PÍ-tu-lo. A book has chapters and so does a television series.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "desenlace",
   "significado": "ending, outcome",
   "pron": "de-sen-LA-the",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «desenlazar», to untie a knot: the knot of the story comes undone at the end.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "editorial",
   "significado": "publishing house",
   "pron": "e-di-to-RYAL",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The company is «la editorial». A newspaper's opinion article is «el editorial».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "agotarse",
   "significado": "to sell out, to run out",
   "pron": "a-go-TAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It takes «se»: «se agotó la edición». It also means running out of strength: «me agoto».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tirada",
   "significado": "print run",
   "pron": "ti-RA-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «tirar», which also means to print. It is the number of copies of an edition.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "verso",
   "significado": "line of poetry",
   "pron": "BER-so",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is written with v but sounds like b: BER-so. Several lines in a row make a stanza.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "rimar",
   "significado": "to rhyme",
   "pron": "rri-MAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The ending sounds rhyme: «luna» and «cuna». The initial r is strong: rri-MAR.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tratar de",
   "significado": "to be about",
   "pron": "tra-TAR de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«El libro trata de un viaje» is the classic way to summarise. «Tratar de» + infinitive means to try.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ambientado en",
   "significado": "set in",
   "pron": "am-byen-TA-do en",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «un relato ambientado en Sevilla». It agrees with the noun: «una novela ambientada en…».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "narra",
   "significado": "narrates (from «narrar»)",
   "pron": "NA-rra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Narrar» means to tell a story. The rr at the start of a word is strong.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "hechos",
   "significado": "events, facts",
   "pron": "E-chos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The h is silent: E-chos. Think of «hecho», done or fact.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
