   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about books",
     "texto": [
      "**Genres.** **Prosa** is running text; **verso** is each line of a poem. In prose there are novels, **relatos** (or cuentos), **leyendas** and **ensayos**. Novels can be historical, adventure, romance (rosa) or crime (negra).\n\n**Inside a story.** The **argumento** is what happens. The **narrador** tells it, in the first or the third person. It can be **ambientado en** a place and a time. Each part is a **capítulo** and the end is the **desenlace**.\n\n**Summarising.** Use the present: «La novela **trata de** un hombre que…», «Es un relato **ambientado en** el Madrid de los años cuarenta».\n\n**The book trade.** The **editorial** publishes or edits the book. The **tirada** is the number of copies; if it sells well, the edition **se agota** (sells out).\n\n**Poetry.** **Versos** rhyme and are recited.\n\n**Careful.** A **librería** sells books; a **biblioteca** lends them."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Summarising a story",
     "texto": [
      "To summarise a book or a film use the **present**, even if the story is set in the past:\n\n- **La novela trata de** un viaje. (**tratar de** + topic)\n- **El relato está ambientado en** una ciudad. (**ambientado en** + place or period)\n- **El protagonista es** un joven **que** busca a su hermano. (**que** introduces the character)\n- **Cuenta la historia de** una familia. (**contar la historia de**)\n\nWith **tratar de**, the topic takes **de**: «trata de amor». With **contar** or **narrar**, it does not: «cuenta un viaje»."
     ],
